#
# output_files/ is where Quartus writes its compilation products
# (PROJECT_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY). It lives at the TEMPLATE ROOT because that is the
# project directory: build_project.tcl runs project_new from here, the committed
# .qsf resolves PROJECT_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY output_files from here, post_flow.tcl
# writes to <git-root>/output_files, and the CI artifact gate reads
# output_files/<rev>.flow.rpt from here. All four converge on this directory.
#
# Most of those products are large, regenerable binaries and must NOT be
# versioned.
#
# EXCEPTION -- this is the whole point of the CI artifact gate: the flow report
# `<revision>.flow.rpt` and its provenance sidecar `<revision>.flow.rpt.provenance.json`
# ARE committed on purpose. Quartus cannot run in CI (node-locked licence), so
# the gate verifies these two files against the commit (see quartus/post_flow.tcl,
# tools/artifact_gate.py and ADR-0006). The negations below re-include exactly
# those two, and NOTHING here may ignore *.flow.rpt or *.provenance.json.

# --- Ignore Quartus build products -------------------------------------------

db/
incremental_db/
*.sof
*.rbf
*.pof
*.qws
*.jdi
*.smsg
*.done
*.pin
*.summary
*.map.*
*.fit.*
*.sta.*

# --- Keep the tracked evidence the gate needs --------------------------------
# These negations MUST stay after the ignore rules above. Do not add any rule
# that would re-ignore the flow report or its provenance sidecar.

!*.flow.rpt
!*.flow.rpt.provenance.json
!*.provenance.json
